# Environment example

Create a `.env.local` file in the project root and fill values from your Supabase project. Never commit `.env.local` to the repo.

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
ADMIN_API_SECRET=a-strong-random-secret-for-api
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_TITLE=Shanti Jewellers
```

Notes:
- SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY must only be used server-side (in API routes). Keep it secret.
- ADMIN_API_SECRET is a simple extra check used by starter admin API endpoints. Replace with proper auth in production.
